## Effort summary
- **Total remaining: ~1–1.5 engineer-weeks**, across ~4–6 IaC PRs.
- **Quick (S, ~½ day combined):** the two 5-min email wins, secure transfer, public-access-disallowed, KV deletion protection + diag logs, Foundry diag logs, AKS Defender profile, PG connection_throttle + log retention.
- **Medium (M, ~2–3 days):** shared-key removal (caller audit), Foundry local-auth + network restriction, storage/KV network rules, diagnostic-logging Policy, trusted-registry policy, governance/SP scope-down, VM encryption-at-host.
- **Heavy (L, ~3–5 days):** private link + private-DNS design across storage/KV/Foundry; AKS read-only-root-filesystem rollout (manifest + app testing). **Biggest single chunk.**
- **Leverage:** the AKS Azure Policy add-on, once in *enforce*, clears the automount/privesc/read-only-FS/limits findings (~150) together — but only after the workload manifests are fixed, so sequence add-on (audit) → fix manifests → enforce.

